<title>CHINA: China insures Three Gorges for 470 mln yuan.</title>
<headline>China insures Three Gorges for 470 mln yuan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The People's Insurance Company of China (PICC) Property, a unit of the PICC Group, has insured the Three Gorges dam power project for 470 million yuan ($56.6 million), the People's Daily Overseas Edition said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The first stage of the project, the damming of the Yangtze River, would be completed by the end of this year, it said.</p>
<p>The newspaper gave no further details.</p>
<p>The Three Gorges project, the world's biggest water control project, will use 14 generating units with total installed capacity of 9,800 megawatts and is scheduled for completion in 2009.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (86-10) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
